   "audioScript": "Commuter: I heard something about the fare system changing in September? Agent: That's right. Paper tickets and tokens are being phased out and replaced by a reloadable tap card called the GoPass. Commuter: How does it work? Agent: You tap it on the reader as you board, and the fare comes off your balance. Commuter: Is there any advantage over just buying tickets? Agent: The biggest change is daily fare capping. Once your taps in a single day add up to the price of a day pass, every ride after that is free, so you never pay more than the day pass no matter how many trips you take. Commuter: Where do I load it? Agent: Online, at any station machine, or at corner stores displaying the GoPass sign. Commuter: I still have a book of paper tickets at home. Agent: Those will be accepted until the end of the year.",
