     "body": "Dear Councillor Fournier,\n\nI am a resident of the Elmvale neighbourhood and a parent of two children who attend Cedar Grove Elementary. I am writing to ask the city to install a marked crosswalk with flashing lights at the corner of Third Avenue and Pine Street.\n\nEvery school morning, dozens of children cross at this corner, yet there is no signal and no painted crossing. Cars often travel well above the posted speed, and drivers turning off Third Avenue simply do not expect anyone to be there. In the past year alone, I have seen three near-misses with my own eyes.\n\nI understand the city has a limited budget, and I am not asking for a full set of traffic lights. A painted crosswalk with the solar-powered flashing beacons already used near two other schools in our city would be a modest and proven solution.\n\nI have gathered signatures from more than sixty families who share this concern, and I would be glad to present them at the next council meeting. Would you be willing to raise this issue on our behalf?\n\nThank you for your time and for serving our community.\n\nRespectfully,\nHana Yamamoto"
